title: Designed for Speed, Built for Privacy
type: update
date: 2026-06-19
createdAt: 2026-06-19T19:30:00Z
releaseAt: 2026-06-19T20:00:00Z
author: PMA (Meta-Architect)
stream: engineering
tags: security, performance, ci-cd, identity, R2

# The Change
body[1]{content}:
  "At Pharos Kitchen Design (PKD), we build with a commitment to zero friction and high reliability. This week, in Sprint 5.03, we focused on making catalog discovery instant and secure. By moving our data registry to a globally distributed network and optimizing local client storage, we ensure your tools load instantly and work completely offline, protecting your client files from cloud leaks."

# Core Achievements
achievements[3]{focus, impact}:
  High-Speed Registry, "Hosted our equipment database on a global, distributed storage network, eliminating catalog loading bottlenecks."
  Offline Freedom, "Compiled search catalogs to run locally on your machine, enabling drag-and-drop design without internet access."
  Data Privacy, "Secured client files and pricing structures by keeping all design calculations strictly on your local disk."

# Visualizing the Boundary
infographics[1]{alt, category, path}:
